#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""RZ/G3L SMARC EVK: write the boot media over the console, without swapping cards (plan/PoC_Workflow_Plan.md 7.3).

  evk-flash doctor     [--image X] [--target emmc|qspi]   check host, connection and files; writes nothing
  evk-flash bootloader {emmc|qspi} [--image X]            SCIF download mode: BL2 + FIP (+ CM33) with Flash Writer
  evk-flash rootfs     --image X                          eMMC boot: the WIC to the eMMC user area from U-Boot (TFTP)
  evk-flash emmc       --image X                          bootloader emmc, then rootfs (works on a board without U-Boot)
  evk-flash clean      [--keep N]                         remove staged chunks of older images from the TFTP root

Images for QSPI or eSD boot on an SD card are written on the host (bmaptool); that is out of scope here.

--image is the <x>.wic.gz in the deploy directory (with <x>.wic.bmap). For `bootloader` it is optional but
recommended: the fip and CM33 firmware that the eSD WIC of the same build embeds are compared with the files to be
written, which proves they come from one build and picks the right CM33 firmware.

Each run leaves data/board-runs/<time>-<command>/ with console.log, report.json and report.md.
Human steps are printed as ">>> 需要你操作：..."; the tool then watches the console, no keyboard input needed.
"""
